  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has delicate, feathery leaves that offer a chance to explore leaf structure and light filtration. Its bright yellow flowers can be used to discuss pollination and the role of color in attracting pollinators. The tree produces long, slender seed pods that demonstrate seed dispersal mechanisms. Its semi-deciduous nature provides an opportunity to study seasonal changes and how trees adapt to different climates.",
